# Server
PORT=8787

# Firebase Admin SDK -- paste the *contents* of the service account JSON
# (Project Settings -> Service Accounts -> Generate new private key), base64-encoded:
#   Windows PowerShell: [Convert]::ToBase64String([IO.File]::ReadAllBytes("service-account.json"))
# Never commit the raw JSON or this .env file.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON_BASE64=
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=sould-ai

# LLM -- baseUrl/model are per-user now (set from the app's Settings > LiteLLM Server and
# Default Model screens, stored on users/{uid} in Firestore). These are optional shared
# fallbacks only: LLM_API_KEY if every user's LiteLLM proxy happens to share one auth key,
# LLM_VISION_MODEL if you want a dedicated vision-capable model for photo-appearance-autofill
# distinct from each user's chosen chat model.
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_VISION_MODEL=

# Event-driven orchestrator (see src/orchestrator/exchange.ts) -- a bounded persona-to-persona
# exchange advances itself across serverless invocations by calling this same deployment's own
# /api/internal/advance-exchange endpoint.
# INTERNAL_BASE_URL: this deployment's own origin (e.g. https://your-backend.vercel.app). Defaults
#   to http://localhost:PORT for local dev if unset.
# INTERNAL_TASK_SECRET: any random string -- shared secret gating that endpoint, since it's
#   server-to-server only and never called by a real signed-in user.
INTERNAL_BASE_URL=
INTERNAL_TASK_SECRET=

# Cloudflare R2 (S3-compatible) -- persona pfp/chat-background photo storage.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID: from the R2 dashboard overview (also the subdomain in the S3 API endpoint).
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: R2 -> Manage API Tokens -> create a token scoped to this bucket.
# R2_BUCKET_NAME: the bucket name.
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL: the bucket's public URL (Settings -> Public access -> r2.dev URL or custom domain),
#   WITHOUT a trailing slash -- uploaded object keys are appended directly to this.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_NAME=
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
